    <div class="flow-node fn-b">
      <div class="flow-label">Night</div>
      <div class="flow-text"><em>Hastara</em> intensifies. <em>Malchus</em> in exile. Sleep = 1/60 of death.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
    <div class="flow-node fn-a">
      <div class="flow-label">Chatzos — Midnight</div>
      <div class="flow-text"><em>Da'as</em> begins to illuminate within <em>Malchus</em>. <em>Binah</em> enters the <em>Gevuros</em>.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
    <div class="flow-node fn-c">
      <div class="flow-label">The Transformation</div>
      <div class="flow-text"><em>Gevuros</em> (= concealments) themselves become <em>Da'as</em>. The concealment within the concealment is revealed.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
    <div class="flow-node fn-d">
      <div class="flow-label">The Rooster's Call</div>
      <div class="flow-text">The Torah cries out: "<em>Ad masai pesayim!</em>" — Awaken, sleepers! This comes from the <em>Gevuros</em> themselves.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
    <div class="flow-node fn-e">
      <div class="flow-label">The Blessing</div>
      <div class="flow-text">"<em>HaNosein laSechvi <strong>Vinah</strong></em>" — through <em>Binah</em>, one distinguishes day from night, light from darkness, good from evil.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

